 nights alike","rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 69\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>69\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 68\u00b0F, and the record is 86\u00b0F (1955, 2005). The low of <strong>49\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Tyler has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Tyler's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Tyler has set <strong class=\"sig\">18 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 73 that chance alone would give, and <strong>106 record highs</strong>, more than the 73 that chance alone would give. The 1910s hold the most record highs of any decade (48). Tyler's all-time high is 110\u00b0F, on August 2, 2011.","t_chg":"Tyler has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 115 complete years: Tyler's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.14\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.03 to +0.26), about +1.8\u00b0F since 1895. Tyler's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.17\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.10 to +0.25), about +2.3\u00b0F since 1895.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 4 of 12 months. Highs rose in 5 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Tyler's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.13 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 43.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 2015 (68.05 in); the driest, 1956 (24.01 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 7 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}